      "content": "Clearing your bags at a transit hub like Singapore or Bangkok usually counts as \"entering\" the country, meaning you will likely need a transit visa or an Entry visa with a brief stay, rather than just a small mainline transit visa. Even if you don't leave the airport building to catch your next flight, the requirement to pass through immigration to collect luggage typically overrides transit-only exemptions. I strongly recommend confirming this specific process with your airline and checking the official immigration portal for each country before finalizing travel plans.",
